---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for the Joe Rossi Umpires Hall of Fame website, historical archive, donations, and events."
  canonicalPath="/terms/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Terms of Use', path: '/terms/' }]}
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <PageHero title="Terms of Use" intro="Terms for responsible use of the Joe Rossi Umpires Hall of Fame website and historical archive." />
    <section class="section">
      <article class="page-surface prose terms-copy">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 25, 2026</p>

        <h2>Site purpose</h2>
        <p>JRHOF.org shares information about the Joe Rossi Umpires Hall of Fame, preserves historical records, recognizes inductees, supports Hall of Fame events, and gives the community ways to contact and support the organization. By using the site, you agree to these terms.</p>

        <h2>Organization</h2>
        <p>The site is published by {site.legalName}, a Colorado 501(c)(3) nonprofit organization, for the {site.name}. The organization’s EIN is {site.ein}.</p>

        <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Please use the site respectfully and only for lawful personal, educational, historical, or community purposes. Do not attempt to disrupt the site, probe or bypass its security, collect other people’s information from it, submit false or harmful information, or use its content in a misleading way. Security researchers can follow the process in our <a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a> file.</p>

        <h2>Historical and archive content</h2>
        <p>Biographies, names, dates, photographs, and event details are preserved from historical records and community sources. The organization works to present information accurately, but the archive may be incomplete or contain errors.</p>
        <p>If you have a documented correction, biography update, portrait concern, or historical material to share, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. The organization reviews submissions before making public changes and decides what to publish.</p>

        <h2>Donations</h2>
        <p>Donations are made to {site.legalName} and are processed by Stripe, a PCI-compliant payment processor. Stripe emails a receipt for every gift; please keep it for your records. Contributions are tax-deductible to the extent allowed by law. If you believe a donation was made in error, email us promptly and we will review it.</p>
        <p>Payments for event seats, golf registrations, mulligans, raffle tickets, and similar items buy goods or services, so they are not fully deductible donations. Raffle ticket purchases are not deductible. Consult a tax advisor about your situation.</p>
        <p>Do not send payment card numbers by email.</p>

        <h2>Events</h2>
        <p>Event dates, locations, prices, registration details, and availability may change. The organization will keep the event pages current, but please confirm details before making plans. Prices, refund terms, and other conditions for a registration or purchase are stated when you buy.</p>
        <p>Hall of Fame events are photographed, and selected photographs are published in the event archive on JRHOF.org. To ask for a photograph of yourself to be reviewed for removal, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>The site links to external websites and documents, including payment and registration providers. External sites are not controlled by the organization, and their content, terms, privacy practices, and availability may differ from JRHOF.org.</p>

        <h2>Intellectual property and content use</h2>
        <p>The Hall of Fame’s name, logos, site text, photographs, portraits, biographies, documents, and archive materials are owned by the organization, contributors, photographers, sponsors, or other rights holders. Do not copy, sell, alter, or republish them without permission, and never in a way that misrepresents the Hall of Fame, the inductees, or the source material. The website’s source code is published separately under the MIT License, which does not cover any of this content.</p>

        <h2>No guarantee</h2>
        <p>The site is provided as a public information and archive resource. The organization does not guarantee that all content is complete, error-free, continuously available, or suitable for every purpose.</p>

        <h2>Limitation of responsibility</h2>
        <p>To the extent allowed by applicable law, the organization is not responsible for losses or damages arising from use of the site, reliance on incomplete historical information, external links, or temporary site unavailability.</p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Colorado.</p>

        <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms, and the date at the top shows the latest version. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>For questions, corrections, or concerns about these terms, email <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a> or use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .terms-copy { margin-inline: auto; }
</style>
